</span></span></span></foreignObject></g><g fill-opacity="1.0" transform="matrix(1.0 0.0 0.0 1.0 20.38 15.19)"><foreignObject style="--ltx-fo-width:33.86em;--ltx-fo-height:10.29em;--ltx-fo-depth:0.19em;font-size:10pt;" height="145.14" overflow="visible" transform="matrix(1 0 0 -1 0 142.45)" width="468.53"><span class="ltx_foreignobject_container"><span class="ltx_foreignobject_content">
<span id="A3.p2.pic1.p1.pic1.2" class="ltx_inline-block ltx_minipage ltx_align_bottom" style="width:33.86em;">
<span id="A3.p2.pic1.p1.pic1.2.1" class="ltx_p">I got a 403 Forbidden error when trying to access <span id="A3.p2.pic1.p1.pic1.2.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_typewriter">flag.txt</span> directly. This means the file exists but we don’t have permission to access it directly. Since there was a file inclusion vulnerability mentioned in the warning on the poems page, I should go back and try to exploit it. The warning showed that the page uses <span id="A3.p2.pic1.p1.pic1.2.1.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_typewriter">file_get_contents()</span> function. Let me go back to the poems page and check if there’s a parameter we can manipulate.</span>
</span></span></span></foreignObject></g></g></svg></span>
</span>
